s="sheet-actions"><button id="speed-slow" aria-pressed="false">Slow · 1 hour / sec</button><button id="speed-grow" aria-pressed="false">Grow · 6 hours / sec</button><button id="speed-fast" aria-pressed="false">Fast-forward · 24 hours / sec</button></div><p id="speed-readout">Start a planet first.</p><p id="speed-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Target is your requested speed; Measured is what your device achieves. Simulation steps stay bounded. Time spent in the background is not caught up.</p><button id="measure-gameplay">Measure gameplay · 10 seconds</button><p>Closes this panel while you play. Pause, menus or leaving the tab cancel the run. Starting a measurement also reads the browser’s available renderer name and drawing-buffer size locally. Nothing is uploaded or saved to disk.</p><section id="gameplay-result" hidden aria-label="Saved gameplay sample"><h3>Saved gameplay sample</h3><button id="copy-gameplay-report">Copy this sample</button><p id="copy-gameplay-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><label id="gameplay-report-label" for="gameplay-report-text" hidden>Local report text. Share only if you choose.</label><textarea id="gameplay-report-text" readonly hidden rows="8" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box" aria-label="Copyable local gameplay report"></textarea><p id="gameplay-result-summary"></p><p id="gameplay-result-readout"></p></section><button id="refresh-speed">Refresh measured speed</button><details id="performance-details"><summary>Performance details · local only</summary><p id="performance-readout">Open while a planet is running to measure.</p><p>Last block of up to 60 frames. P95 is the 95th-percentile frame interval; max and the &gt;50 ms count catch rarer stalls. Physics is per active frame, not tick. Render is elapsed call time, including driver waits, not GPU time. These are not touch-latency measurements. Nothing is uploaded; closing stops measurement.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="god-sheet" aria-labelledby="god-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="god-title">God tools · deliberate interventions</h2><button id="close-god">Close</button></div><p id="god-target">Select a patch first.</p><p id="god-availability" role="status" aria-live="polite" style="white-space:pre-line"></p><div id="god-actions"><button id="god-wave">Send wave</button><button id="god-heat">Strike lightning</button><button id="god-scorch" disabled>Scorch · Sandbox</button><button id="god-ignite" disabled>Ignite detritus · Origin</button></div><button id="find-detritus">Find dead organic matter</button><button id="cancel-detritus" hidden>Cancel search</button><button id="god-refresh">Refresh target</button><p id="god-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details id="ignition-ledger" hidden><summary>Last ignition this session · not saved history</summary><p>Fuel heat is calibrated at 30 MJ per kg carbon for gameplay, not measured fuel chemistry. This record is local runtime evidence, not a saved event history, and may be from another planet opened this session.</p><p id="ignition-summary"></p><pre id="ignition-receipt" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details><details id="god-help"><summary>How these tools work</summary><p>Wave pushes existing water into up to six neighboring patches: at most 25% of this patch’s water, capped at 1 m equivalent. No water creation or terrain erosion.</p><p>Lightning adds a local heat impulse of up to 40°C (capped at 500 K). This is an external god power, not a full lightning simulation. Life responds through actual temperature and flooding rules over time, not guaranteed destruction.</p><p>Scorch destroys 75% of dry Sandbox cover and adds up to 40°C. It can kill rabbits through existing heat limits. This is external destruction, not fire chemistry; no guaranteed recovery.</p><p>Origin only: ignite exposed dead carbon on a completely dry patch. This one-shot oxidation consumes existing detritus and oxygen, adds carbon dioxide and heat, and stops at its fuel, oxygen or temperature limit. It does not directly burn living colonies, spread wildfire or unlock fire-adapted life. Heat can affect life afterward. Wet ground cannot ignite. Use Find dead organic matter to navigate to existing fuel (dry eligible patches are preferred), then inspect Life snapshot. Wet fuel remains wet; use Water − if you deliberately want to expose it. Pause to hold conditions, then reopen or refresh this panel: water can return while time runs. Nothing is automatically drained or seeded, and ignition does not promise a benefit.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="life-sheet" aria-labelledby="life-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="life-title">Life in this patch</h2><button id="close-life">Close</button></div><button id="watch-patch">Watch this patch · 10 seconds</button><p class="life-note">Closes this sheet to watch real photosynthesis, grazing and net living biomass here while time runs. Does not unpause or speed up the world. Menus, navigation or changing tabs stop observation. Biological carbon returned to air excludes movement respiration and god tools. Net biomass includes all local changes, not growth alone.</p><button id="find-feeding">Find recorded feeding</button><button id="cancel-feeding" hidden>Cancel search</button><p id="feeding-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="life-note">Amber dots mark living grazing-capable microbes with past feeding, not animals or eating now.</p><p id="life-summary" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="life-conditions"></p><section id="competition-panel" hidden aria-labelledby="competition-title"><h3 id="competition-title">Competition at a glance</h3><p id="life-competition" style="white-space:pre-line"></p></section><section id="living-traits" hidden aria-label="Living traits"><b>Living traits · current colonies</b><p id="living-traits-copy"></p><p class="life-note">Potential comes from inherited structure plus living support. Compatibility is not measured photosynthesis or a growth guarantee; dry land is not supported. Biomass trend is reported separately.</p></section><div id="life-cohorts"></div><div id="fine-water" hidden><p>Selected patch water · fine adjustment. Time keeps running unless paused.</p><button id="water-minus">−0.1 m water</button> <button id="water-plus">+0.1 m water</button><div id="target-water" hidden><p>Set this patch to an explicit depth. This supplies or removes water once, not automatic care.</p><label for="water-target">Target depth (metres, 0–5)</label><input id="water-target" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="5" step="any" value="0.5"><button id="water-target-apply">Set depth</button> <button id="water-shallow">Set 0.5 m</button><button id="make-pond">Shape basin + add water</button><p>Shapes up to 19 terrain patches: a level floor and dry rim raised at least 17 m above it. Supplies 15 m water to the floor and drains the rim once. Existing life is not replaced; changed terrain/water can affect it. No automatic refill.</p></div><p id="water-feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></div><button id="refresh-life">Refresh snapshot</button><p id="life-glossary" class="life-note"></p><p class="life-note">Colony IDs are serial identifiers, not a count of living colonies or species. Births since start includes colonies that later died. Generation counts descent steps from a seeded ancestor. Parent IDs may refer to colonies no longer alive.</p></dialog><section id="guide" hidden><button id="close-guide">Close</button><h2 id="guide-heading">Sandbox habitat guide</h2><div id="goal-card" aria-live="polite"><h3 id="goal-title">Start a habitat</h3><p id="goal-text">Start the game, then check your habitat for a suggested next step.</p></div><div class="guide-actions"><button id="check-habitat">Check habitat</button><button id="guide-land">Find land</button><button id="repeat-guide">First steps</button></div><p><span id="mode-explanation">This sandbox starts with plants and rabbits. It does not yet evolve simple life into new plant or animal groups. Suggestions reflect the current planet, not required levels or guaranteed survival.</span></p><details id="manual"><summary>Controls and field notes</summary><div id="origin-fields" hidden><p>Turquoise mats mark real microbial biomass. Tap <b>Habitat</b> to find shallow water; <b>Seed</b> introduces an existing colony. <b>Nutr. +</b> is a deliberate external nutrient input, not food created by the ecosystem.</p><p>Simple seeds need 0.2–50 m water above 0°C, usable light and resources. Evolved producers with actual paid support and inherited structure can exploit thinner liquid films; the 15–20 cm transition also permits partial aquatic growth. No photosynthesis occurs when dry or frozen. Grazing and movement still require aquatic conditions. Inspect shows carbon biomass, nutrients and the dominant living colony. Descendants can develop aquatic producer forms: cushion, rosette, ribbon, branching and canopy. Shapes follow inherited traits and actual support tissue; these are not terrestrial plant species or animals.</p><p><b>Habitat care:</b> Use <b>Find habitat → Shape nursery → Seed colony → Watch life</b> for a shallow starting patch. Nursery shapes a 5 m center beside a 15 m reservoir and dry rim; it supplies water once, not new organisms. Press Play if paused. The older level 15 m basin is still available in Life snapshot. Inspect shallow patches as water changes. For routine replenishment, a <b>Water +</b> tap adds 1 m to the selected patch. <b>Water −</b> removes up to 1 m per tap from only the selected patch, or 5 m per second while painting; it never drains neighbors. Both water brushes are external interventions, not rainfall or evaporation. For precision, open <b>Life snapshot</b> and choose <b>Set 0.5 m</b>. Both supply water once: there is no automatic refill or guaranteed evolution.</p></div><div id="sandbox-fields"><p><b>Read the map:</b> tan is bare land, blue is water, green is vegetation, and orange dots mark living rabbits. Close-up sprouts show real vegetated patches, not individual plant counts; they grow with coverage and shrink when grazed. Rabbit models stand on the surface when you zoom close.</p><p><b>1. Find your land.</b> Tap <b>Land</b> below the game to jump to dry ground. Use <b>＋</b> to get close and <b>Globe</b> to return to a whole-planet view.</p><p><b>2. Shape a habitat.</b> Use Land +/− and Water +/−. Dry land supports rabbits; deep water does not. Pause while sculpting. Water − removes up to 1 m per tap from the selected patch only (5 m per second held), never neighboring water. Water and land brushes respond to how long you hold, not simulation speed. Inspect shows water depth.</p><p><b>3. Plant the land.</b> Choose Plants and paint patches of vegetation. Rabbits eat it, so establish food before adding animals.</p><p><b>4. Add rabbits.</b> Choose Rabbits, then tap suitable land. Watch the population and inspect the surface temperature. This prototype currently has vegetation and rabbits, not a full multi-species ecosystem.</p></div><p><b>Always daylight</b> keeps the side you are viewing lit while the climate simulation continues. You can change the view in the planet menu.</p><p>Tap menu buttons and the tool buttons inside the game. Choose a tool, then touch the planet to use it.</p><p><b>Pinch with two fingers</b> to zoom smoothly. In <b>Navigate</b> mode, drag one finger to explore and tap to use a menu or selected tool. Switch to <b>Paint</b> to brush plants or terrain by dragging. Pinching never finishes as a tool tap. Zoom +/− also works.</p><p>Landscape gives you more room. Full screen hides the browser bars. The game automatically resizes when you rotate.</p><p><b>More → Save / Load:</b> Save keeps one planet in this browser on this device, including its ecosystem. It is not a cloud backup. Wait for the Saved message before closing. Clearing site data or using a private browsing session can remove it. Load replaces your unsaved world.</p><p><b>Mobile detail:</b> New browser planets use a lighter grid for smoother play and smaller saves. Existing saved worlds keep their original grid detail when loaded.</p><p>Pause, settings and tool details are now in the game, above the planet. Open <b>More → Speed / fast-forward</b> to choose a target of 1, 6 or 24 simulated hours per real second. The top pace button also cycles these targets. Achieved speed is measured separately and may be lower on your device. New worlds start with the 6-hour target; saved worlds keep their requested pace. Pause to sculpt or inspect. Faster time also dries water faster, so watch your habitat.</p></details><a href="qa.html">Executed gameplay tests</a> · <a href="source.html">GPL source</a> · <a href="LICENSE">License</a></section><aside id="gameplay-measure-status" hidden aria-live="polite"><span id="gameplay-measure-message"></span><button id="cancel-gameplay-measure">Cancel</button></aside></main><script src="copy-report.js"></script><script src="renderer-info.js"></script><script src="gameplay-measure.js"></script><script src="touch-controls.js"></script><script src="stella-storage.js"></script><script src="life-trend.js"></script><script src="patch-watch.js"></script><script>
